+    The one transport both axis moves share (charter 190): the width layer
+    (``apply_center_width_calibration``) and the consensus bridge's
+    recentering (``cross_consensus.shift_probability``, a pure shift: lam 1).
+    An interior bucket is a point on its centre, split linearly between the
+    two centres it lands between, and anything past either end accumulates
+    in that end bucket.  A declared open end bucket is a tail
+    (``_open_edge_tail_landing``).  Adds into ``moved`` in place and returns
+    ``(side, scale, released)`` for a tail, None for a point.
